{"study_accession":"PRJNA1280065","secondary_study_accession":"SRP593374","title":"Human Endogenous Retroviruses Drive Type-I Interferon Signaling activation in Early Rheumatoid Arthritis","description":"Substantial reactivation of HERVs was observed in both synovial tissues and PBMCs from early RA patients. Differentially expressed HERVs regulate adjacent ISGs expression by providing cis-regulatory elements. Moreover, excessive cytoplasmic HERVs trigger a type I interferon (IFN-I) response through the dsRNA-RIG-I-IRF3-IFN-I axis. Targeting endogenous retroviruses exhibited potential therapeutic benefits in both CIA mouse models and RA patient-derived ex vivo models. Specifically, the IFN-I inducible HERV.MLT2B2, a novel primate-specific retroelement, acts as a key driver of the antiviral gene IFI44L, establishing a positive feedback loop that amplifies IFN-I signaling. Overall design: The discovery cohort included six early RA patients, six osteoarthritis (OA) patients, and six healthy controls, from whom PBMCs were isolated for RNA sequencing analysis.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN49514446","study_accession":"PRJNA1280065","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"RA6","description":"RA6","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9058169","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-09","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["tissue","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["subject status","early RA patient"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR34075906","experiment_accession":"SRX29270778","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":18825813,"base_count":5483631896,"first_public":"2026-06-09","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM9058169: RA6 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN49514447","study_accession":"PRJNA12800